{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "03107",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.66,
      "end_seconds": 4.6,
      "duration_seconds": 3.94,
      "text": "Hello, doctor. I think it's my turn."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 6.55,
      "end_seconds": 10.18,
      "duration_seconds": 3.63,
      "text": "Yes, have a seat. Tell me what's going on."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 10.69,
      "end_seconds": 14.59,
      "duration_seconds": 3.9,
      "text": "I've been dealing with ringing in the ears."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 15.36,
      "end_seconds": 18.34,
      "duration_seconds": 2.98,
      "text": "How long has it been like this?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 20.07,
      "end_seconds": 29.37,
      "duration_seconds": 9.3,
      "text": "Since this morning, that's when it began. I just want to get back to normal, really."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 29.91,
      "end_seconds": 32.57,
      "duration_seconds": 2.66,
      "text": "Does anything else come with it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 34.13,
      "end_seconds": 46.96,
      "duration_seconds": 12.83,
      "text": "Hearing getting worse in both ears goes along with it, most of the time. The hearing getting worse in both ears? That's been for six months."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 56.98,
      "end_seconds": 59.36,
      "duration_seconds": 2.38,
      "text": "Let me take your readings now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 71.59,
      "end_seconds": 74.52,
      "duration_seconds": 2.93,
      "text": "That's it, just a little longer..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 87.91,
      "end_seconds": 100.07,
      "duration_seconds": 12.16,
      "text": "Okay: height 170 centimetres, respiratory rate 14. And heart rate 73, weight 66 kilos, temp 36.5 degrees, BMI works out to 22.8, BP is 128 over 80."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 101.84,
      "end_seconds": 105.12,
      "duration_seconds": 3.28,
      "text": "Right, let's have a proper look at you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 106.06,
      "end_seconds": 107.48,
      "duration_seconds": 1.42,
      "text": "Does that hurt?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 121.57,
      "end_seconds": 127.82,
      "duration_seconds": 6.25,
      "text": "Both ear drums look normal and the tuning fork is heard better through the bone."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 137.67,
      "end_seconds": 139.05,
      "duration_seconds": 1.38,
      "text": "Fine by me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 141.54,
      "end_seconds": 145.93,
      "duration_seconds": 4.39,
      "text": "You can relax now. Have you noticed vertigo or discharge?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 147.99,
      "end_seconds": 152.29,
      "duration_seconds": 4.3,
      "text": "No, you know, none of those at all."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 153.07,
      "end_seconds": 155.12,
      "duration_seconds": 2.05,
      "text": "Any sign of ear pain?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 156.48,
      "end_seconds": 160.47,
      "duration_seconds": 3.99,
      "text": "No, I haven't had any ear pain."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 162.36,
      "end_seconds": 163.72,
      "duration_seconds": 1.36,
      "text": "Neurologically, anything strange?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 165.02,
      "end_seconds": 169.12,
      "duration_seconds": 4.1,
      "text": "So, um, no, that's all normal."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 170.98,
      "end_seconds": 174.48,
      "duration_seconds": 3.5,
      "text": "How about your heart, any problems like that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 175.98,
      "end_seconds": 180.96,
      "duration_seconds": 4.98,
      "text": "My heart's been fine, as far as I know."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 181.81,
      "end_seconds": 184.22,
      "duration_seconds": 2.41,
      "text": "What's on your current medicine list?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 185.7,
      "end_seconds": 190.1,
      "duration_seconds": 4.4,
      "text": "I take tamsulosin, at night for the prostate."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 191.58,
      "end_seconds": 194.01,
      "duration_seconds": 2.43,
      "text": "How much do you take?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 195.94,
      "end_seconds": 215.67,
      "duration_seconds": 19.73,
      "text": "It's 0.4 milligrams. Well, it's metformin, 500 milligrams, twice a day. I thought it would sort itself out, but it hasn't. I wasn't sure whether to come in at all, to be honest."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 217.31,
      "end_seconds": 220.91,
      "duration_seconds": 3.6,
      "text": "Any health conditions I should have on record?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 221.74,
      "end_seconds": 233.96,
      "duration_seconds": 12.22,
      "text": "I've had an enlarged prostate, yes. I looked a few things up online, and that probably didn't help. I have diabetes, for five years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 235.44,
      "end_seconds": 238.22,
      "duration_seconds": 2.78,
      "text": "Have you got any known allergies?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 239.05,
      "end_seconds": 242.34,
      "duration_seconds": 3.29,
      "text": "I don't think I have any, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 243.7,
      "end_seconds": 246.56,
      "duration_seconds": 2.86,
      "text": "Now some background about your lifestyle."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 248.54,
      "end_seconds": 257.3,
      "duration_seconds": 8.76,
      "text": "I walk the dog every morning. Lots of rice, lentils and some fruit. My partner and our baby."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 273.98,
      "end_seconds": 280.21,
      "duration_seconds": 6.23,
      "text": "Putting it all together, this looks most like a conductive hearing loss, possibly otosclerosis."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 282.09,
      "end_seconds": 284.9,
      "duration_seconds": 2.81,
      "text": "What are the odds it's serious?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 286.21,
      "end_seconds": 297.18,
      "duration_seconds": 10.97,
      "text": "Nothing I've seen today points to an emergency. It looks like a conductive hearing loss, possibly otosclerosis, but I'd like to confirm."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 313.31,
      "end_seconds": 316.85,
      "duration_seconds": 3.54,
      "text": "Let's get a hearing test, for hearing loss."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 317.89,
      "end_seconds": 321.05,
      "duration_seconds": 3.16,
      "text": "Where would I go for that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 325.79,
      "end_seconds": 343.84,
      "duration_seconds": 18.05,
      "text": "A hearing aid or an operation are both options after the tests. If the symptoms get worse, or you feel really unwell, please come to the emergency department. Let's plan a check after the tests. That's all from me. Any questions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 345.21,
      "end_seconds": 349.79,
      "duration_seconds": 4.58,
      "text": "Uh, okay, that makes sense. Thanks for explaining."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 356.15,
      "end_seconds": 357.35,
      "duration_seconds": 1.2,
      "text": "Goodbye for now."
    }
  ]
}